<%# Pick/Unpick button. It was inline on Discover; it became a partial because
    the hero and the row's cards need the same behavior.

    The three conditions mirror the model's rules (CLAUDE.md § Authorization):
    you do not pick your own Epic, and there is one Pick per user per Epic.

    The turbo_frame_tag is the target of PicksController's turbo_stream: without
    it a click would reload the whole page and the user would lose their place in
    the list. The id includes the epic because the same Epic can appear more than
    once on a page (Discover's hero + rail).

    When there is no button to show, the Epic page explains why: without that the
    slot sits empty and "you cannot pick this" is indistinguishable from "it
    broke" — which is exactly what happened with someone's own Epic. Lists say
    nothing: repeated per row it would be noise, and there the empty slot reads
    against the rows that do have one.

    Locals: epic. Optional: compact (true in lists and cards, where the hero's
    full pill does not fit, and where the note is left out). %>
<% compact = local_assigns[:compact] %>
<% size = compact ? "px-3 py-1 text-xs" : "px-4 py-2 text-sm" %>

<%= turbo_frame_tag dom_id(epic, :pick_button), target: "_top" do %>
  <% if current_user && current_user.id != epic.user_id %>
    <% if picked_epic_ids.include?(epic.id) %>
      <%= button_to "Picked ✓", epic_pick_path(epic), method: :delete,
            form: { class: "inline-block" },
            class: "rounded-full border border-lime-accent/40 #{size} font-semibold text-lime-accent hover:bg-lime-accent/10" %>
    <% else %>
      <%= button_to "Pick", epic_pick_path(epic), method: :post,
            form: { class: "inline-block" },
            class: "rounded-full bg-lime-accent #{size} font-semibold text-neutral-950 hover:bg-lime-bright" %>
    <% end %>
  <% elsif !compact %>
    <p class="text-xs text-neutral-500">
      <% if current_user %>
        <em>This Epic is yours — Pick is for other people’s Epics.</em>
      <% else %>
        <em>Sign in to pick this Epic.</em>
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
